@*
    The one moment of the interview that is genuinely the client's decision and also the join
    between two entries of the map: what follows the button is the next kind of request, asked
    without leaving the page, until the map is spent.
*@

<div class="sealed">
    <h2>@Named is @(Revising ? "revised" : "written")</h2>

    <p>
        What it is, what it reaches for, how it works &mdash; all settled.
        @if (Revising)
        {
            @*
                An agent taken out of the domain to be corrected is not the last entry of a map: no
                map was drawn today and calling it the last of one reports a place in a list the
                client never dictated. What is true is smaller and is the whole of what they need —
                it goes back where it came from and they go on going over the rest.
            *@
            <text>Put it back in the domain and carry on going over the others.</text>
        }
        else if (Remaining > 0)
        {
            <text>
                Put it in the domain and we go on to @Next &mdash;
                @(Remaining == 1 ? "the last one left" : $"{Remaining} left") on the map.
            </text>
        }
        else
        {
            <text>
                It is the last on the map. Put it in the domain and the whole of it is there to be
                reviewed and taken away.
            </text>
        }
    </p>

    <div class="sealed-actions">
        @Back

        @Keep

        <button class="primary" @onclick="() => OnAccept.InvokeAsync()" disabled="@Busy">
            @(Revising ? "Back into the domain" : Remaining > 0 ? "Into the domain, then the next" : "Into the domain")
        </button>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The interview whose agent has just been finished.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public InterviewState State { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>
    /// The way back into the agent, beside the button that lets it out.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? Back { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Taking the work away, beside the button that lets the agent into the domain.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? Keep { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the commit is already under way.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Busy { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Raised when the client lets the agent into the domain.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnAccept { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// What to call the finished agent: its button, which is the client's own phrase for it.
    /// </summary>
    private string Named => State.Intent.Label ?? State.Intent.Name ?? "This agent";

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether this agent came out of the domain to be corrected rather than out of a map drawn
    /// today.
    /// </summary>
    private bool Revising => State.Revision is not null;

    /// <summary>
    /// How many entries of the map have no agent yet, this one excluded.
    /// </summary>
    private int Remaining => State.Map.Count - State.At - 1;

    /// <summary>
    /// What the next entry is called.
    /// </summary>
    private string Next =>
        State.At + 1 < State.Map.Count
            ? State.Map[State.At + 1].Label ?? State.Map[State.At + 1].Name ?? "the next one"
            : "the next one";
}
